{"title":"G4.6 → G4.7 Combined Physical Qualification Execution-Order Amendment v0.1"}
</properties>
<iconMetadata>{"type":"emoji","emoji":"🔁"}</iconMetadata>
<content>
<callout icon="🔁" color="blue_bg">
	**Execution-order amendment — 2026-10-08.** G4.6 automated/code qualification is complete enough to start G4.7 implementation, while G4.6 physical evidence remains intentionally deferred. This amendment changes execution order only; it does **not** manufacture G4.6 Gate PASS and does not remove any physical obligation.
</callout>
# 1. Exact Upstream Boundary
Repository: `Mostorm-Labs/axiom`
Post-G4.6 execution branch / G4.7 starting branch:
- `codex/g4-7-development`
- exact starting revision: `68b925e53b092657f3415c3d3992a451a8515598`
G4.6-C exact automation/evidence ancestry:
- G4.6-C result revision recorded in branch: `5194d5ccf186e49a45311b39a831d1c9460e043e`
- G4.6-C status: `PASS_AUTOMATION_WITH_PHYSICAL_BLOCKERS`
- qualification bundle: 11/11 automated scenarios PASS
- deterministic replay: 11/11 PASS
- frozen CTest: 69/69 PASS
- contract tests: 14/14 PASS
- official G4.6 Gate PASS: **not claimed**
Pending G4.6 obligations preserved for later combined physical qualification:
- G46C-PHYS-002 Windows fixed physical checklist
- G46C-PHYS-002 Web fixed physical checklist
- G46C-PHYS-002 Android fixed physical checklist
- G46C-COEXIST-004 platform Pen/Laser + editing-overlay coexistence observations
- missing dedicated provider refs remain evidence debt, not evidence of PASS
# 2. Superseded Execution Timing
The old G4.7 roadmap required **G4.6 Gate PASS before G4.7-00**.
For implementation ordering only, that requirement is superseded by:
> G4.7 P32 may start from the exact post-G4.6 automated/evidence boundary above, provided G4.6 physical obligations remain open and are carried into the Combined G4 Physical Qualification.
This does **not** supersede the requirement that physical evidence must be closed before final Gate closure and before G5 consumes a formally accepted post-G4.7 baseline.
# 3. Combined Physical Qualification Strategy
G4.7 implementation proceeds through code-complete, automated-verification-complete and qualification-artifact-ready state first.
After G4.7 reaches that state, one combined physical qualification phase validates both:
- remaining G4.6 interaction/presentation obligations; and
- G4.7 RichText display/font/zoom/DPR/cross-platform obligations.
Combined qualification must bind exact result/build/platform/device/font identities.
Terminal implementation state before combined physical qualification:
`READY_FOR_COMBINED_G4_PHYSICAL_QUALIFICATION`
This state is **not**:
- G4.6 Gate PASS
- G4.7 Gate PASS
- G5 entry authorization
# 4. G4.7 Repo Reality Frozen for P31
At `68b925e53b092657f3415c3d3992a451a8515598`:
- canonical RichText schema exists at `schema/axiom/v1/proto/auditoryworks/axiom/v1/rich_text.proto`;
- RuntimeScene and DirectReferenceSource already carry RichText as a renderer-neutral semantic/reference command;
- current `BoundsSystem` still uses a heuristic RichText width/height estimate and therefore must be replaced by derived production layout bounds;
- current common Skia scene renderer does not yet materialize production RichText drawing;
- locked `r1-full-skia-sdk.lock.json` profile `r1-full-v1` has `richtext=true`, HarfBuzz and ICU on required targets;
- POC-04 contains a working SkParagraph/SkUnicode ICU reference implementation and deterministic/font-resource fixtures;
- `deps.lock.json` pins Roboto Regular and Noto Sans CJK subset hashes.
Therefore G4.7 does not need a new text-stack selection decision.
# 5. Frozen Text Implementation Decisions
Production internal text stack:
- locked R1 Full Skia SDK only;
- SkParagraph + SkShaper + SkUnicode ICU / bundled HarfBuzz+ICU capabilities;
- no Skia rebuild;
- no renderer-specific/native font handles in stable Scene/Public contracts.
Font identity:
- consume canonical `TextStyle.font_resource_id`;
- use explicit runtime FontResource provider/resolver seam;
- use bundled hash-pinned Roboto Regular + Noto Sans CJK subset for deterministic CI/golden/qualification corpus;
- no OS/browser implicit fallback;
- no nearest-weight or synthetic bold/italic substitution when exact face is unavailable.
Layout constraint:
- no new RichText canonical width/height/TextBox fields;
- `RichTextLayoutService` accepts an explicit runtime `LayoutContext/Constraint`;
- verification/playground may provide deterministic fixed-width contexts;
- production code must only consume an accepted container/runtime constraint source and must not infer Product Shell state.
Unicode qualification scope:
- blocking automated corpus: Latin, numbers/punctuation, CJK, mixed Latin+CJK, combining marks;
- emoji is required where the pinned font corpus contains the exact glyph; missing glyph otherwise follows explicit degraded-resource diagnostics;
- explicit bidi paragraph-direction schema / full RTL product semantics remain deferred and do not block G4.7 unless existing accepted canonical input already requires them.
# 6. G4.7 P32 Completion Boundary
P32 must complete:
- production renderer-neutral RichText layout runtime;
- exact font resource/profile behavior;
- Scene bounds/spatial/resource invalidation integration;
- Direct/NonTiled reference + production Skia render integration;
- EditRichText locality and negative controls;
- deterministic text workload corpus;
- Text Performance Playground;
- structured-grid proxy;
- Windows/Web/Android qualification hooks and artifacts.
P32 must **not** wait for physical human/device observation after those artifacts are ready.
P32 returns only when:
- code complete;
- required automated verification passes;
- qualification bundle is ready;
- result/evidence is reviewer-accessible;
- terminal status = `READY_FOR_COMBINED_G4_PHYSICAL_QUALIFICATION`;
or when an explicit frozen blocker is reached.
# 7. Final Gate Boundary Preserved
Combined physical qualification remains mandatory before:
- closing the deferred G4.6 physical obligations;
- claiming G4.7 Gate PASS;
- authorizing G5 from a formally accepted G4.7 baseline.
G4.7 still does not implement G6 TextEditSession, caret/selection interaction, IME composition, platform editor overlays, Clipboard, ExternalSurface, Table semantics or new RichText sizing schema.
</content>
</page>

